        "matrix-multiplication-and-the-identity",
        "transformations-of-the-unit-square"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "formulae",
          "groups": [
            {
              "title": "Calculus",
              "colour": "#6d28d9",
              "items": [
                {
                  "name": "Differentiating a power",
                  "formula": "$y = kx^n \\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = knx^{n-1}$",
                  "symbols": "For any integer $n$; a constant differentiates to $0$. Expand brackets and split fractions first."
                },
                {
                  "name": "Tangent and normal",
                  "formula": "$m_{\\text{normal}} = -\\dfrac{1}{m_{\\text{tangent}}}$",
                  "symbols": "Find $m$ from $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at the point, then use $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Stationary points",
                  "formula": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 0$",
                  "symbols": "Then $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} > 0$ is a minimum and $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} < 0$ a maximum"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Increasing and decreasing",
                  "formula": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} > 0$ increasing, $\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} < 0$ decreasing"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Algebra",
              "colour": "#1d4ed8",
              "items": [
                {
                  "name": "The factor theorem",
                  "formula": "$f(a) = 0 \\iff (x - a) \\text{ is a factor of } f(x)$",
                  "symbols": "And for a rational root: $f\\left(\\tfrac{b}{a}\\right) = 0 \\iff (ax - b)$ is a factor"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Coordinate geometry",
              "colour": "#c2410c",
              "items": [
                {
                  "name": "Distance between two points",
                  "formula": "$\\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$",
                  "symbols": "Pythagoras on the change in $x$ and the change in $y$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Midpoint",
                  "formula": "$\\left(\\dfrac{x_1 + x_2}{2},\\ \\dfrac{y_1 + y_2}{2}\\right)$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Perpendicular gradients",
                  "formula": "$m_1 \\times m_2 = -1$"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Matrices",
              "colour": "#047857",
              "items": [
                {
                  "name": "The identity matrix",
                  "formula": "$I = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$",
                  "symbols": "Leaves every point where it is: $IA = AI = A$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Enlargement, scale factor $k$, centre the origin",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Rotation 90° anticlockwise about the origin",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Rotation 180° about the origin",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Rotation 270° anticlockwise (90° clockwise) about the origin",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Reflection in $x = 0$, the $y$-axis",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Reflection in $y = 0$, the $x$-axis",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Reflection in $y = x$",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Reflection in $y = -x$",
                  "formula": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "body": "**Checking a matrix.** The first column is where $(1, 0)$ goes and the second is where $(0, 1)$ goes. For a rotation of $90^\\circ$ anticlockwise, $(1, 0)$ moves to $(0, 1)$ and $(0, 1)$ to $(-1, 0)$, which gives the columns $\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$. Two transformations in turn, $A$ then $B$, are the single matrix $BA$: the first one goes on the right."
        }
      ],
      "applications": [
        {
          "title": "Computer graphics",
          "body": "Every time a game turns or mirrors a character, it multiplies each point by a matrix like these. Two moves in a row are one matrix multiplied by another."
        },
        {
          "title": "Getting the most from a sheet of card",
          "body": "Cutting squares from the corners of a sheet to fold a box, the volume is a cubic in the square's side. Setting $\\dfrac{dV}{dx} = 0$ finds the size that holds the most."
